   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The Scotch Gambit. A key practical point: when you sense your opponent is entering a line you don't know and fear getting crushed in the main theory, a quiet move that accepts a slightly worse but solid position keeps you on the board. The principled tries are the knight to f6, meeting e5 with d5, or the bishop to c5."
